WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:04.810
By Hollywood standards, Robert Pattinson has
been around for what seems like a lifetime

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:05.300
already.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.640
It's been 14 years since Pattinson made his
big-screen debut in Harry Potter and the Goblet

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:13.340
of Fire, and not even a decade has passed
since he stole the hearts of tweens the world

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.860
over as the Twilight saga's brooding vampire
Edward Cullen.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.000
Since then, Pattinson has carved out one of
the most intriguing careers in Hollywood by

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.300
continuing to claim challenging and quirky
roles in independent films.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:28.760
When it was announced that Pattinson was returning
to big franchise movies by claiming the coveted

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.850
lead in Warner Bros.' superhero flick The
Batman, the internet nearly imploded at the

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:35.720
prospect of Pattinson donning the cape to
play the Dark Knight.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:40.160
While there were some positive reactions,
many fans were quite displeased at the casting

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:40.660
news.

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:41.920
"Take it.

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:43.880
They'll hate you for it, but that's the point
of Batman.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.400
He can be the outcast."

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:51.300
It turns out that die-hard Bat-fans weren't
the only ones miffed when that news broke.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.900
In a recent interview with Variety, Pattinson
said he was also pretty upset about the news,

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.230
but for a totally different reason.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:57.720
He said:

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:00.600
"When that thing leaked, I was f---ing furious.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:01.989
Everyone was so upset.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:03.142
Everyone was panicking from my team.

00:01:03.142 --> 00:01:05.720
I sort of thought that had blown up the whole
thing."

00:01:06.470 --> 00:01:10.760
It seems that when Variety initially broke
the casting exclusive, the deal to bring Pattinson

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.380
to Gotham was far from done.

00:01:12.680 --> 00:01:16.960
In fact, the actor hadn't yet officially auditioned
for the role, and talks with Warner Bros.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.860
and The Batman director Matt Reeves were very
much still ongoing.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:24.080
The reason Pattinson was so upset was because
he really wanted the part, and was afraid

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:28.360
all the premature chatter from internet fandom
might actually scare Warner Bros. away from

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:28.940
casting him.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.580
On the day the Batman news broke, Pattinson
found himself compulsively Googling his own

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.480
name for news about the expected fallout.

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:40.440
Luckily, Warner Bros. eventually stood up
for its casting decision regarding The Batman,

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.000
confirming Pattinson would indeed portray
the Caped Crusader in Reeves' upcoming film.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.600
Ironically, even after flipping out about
someone else leaking his involvement with

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.790
The Batman before it was a done deal, Pattinson
himself accidentally let a spoiler slip for

00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:57.000
another hotly anticipated Warner Bros. movie:
Todd Phillips' Joker.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.751
During his chat with Variety, Pattinson was
said to have made a "mundane comment" about

00:02:00.751 --> 00:02:05.500
Joker star Joaquin Phoenix before "asking
to retract it," as it apparently spoiled something

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.090
in the film, even if it was relatively minor.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:11.600
The actor admitted that he's not used to thinking
about spoilers during interviews.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:12.200
He said:

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:12.960
"Oh s---.

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:14.640
I definitely should not say that.

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.620
I'm so used to pretty art-house movies, where
you can watch the movie three times and still

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:19.580
not know what it's about."

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.780
Pattinson might just be an inspired casting
choice who could be more than capable of bringing

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.820
pathos and physicality to one of the most
complicated superheroes ever created.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:33.000
If you don't believe that, look past Pattinson's
Twilight years and seek out some of the indie

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.360
gems he's been cranking out of late, particularly
the sci-fi flick High Life.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.880
Reeves and company have yet to announce any
more casting for The Batman, which has not

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:42.189
yet begun filming.

00:02:42.189 --> 00:02:46.459
It's slated to hit theaters in June 2021,
so we've got a bit of a wait ahead to see

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:49.960
what Pattinson brings to the complex dual
roles of Bruce Wayne and Batman.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.209
Here's hoping he delivers the goods when The
Batman finally swings into action in a couple

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:54.740
of years.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:02:56.160
But fear not, Team Pattinson.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:00.280
The actor's chiseled features will be more
than visible on big screens in the intervening

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.959
years, with Robert Eggers' The Lighthouse
on the immediate horizon and David Michôd's

00:03:04.960 --> 00:03:06.560
The King hitting Netflix soon after.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:10.880
Pattinson is also hard at work shooting Christopher
Nolan's Tenet this very moment, with that

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:12.760
film scheduled to hit theaters next year.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:19.620
"I'm quite glad I'm doing a Chris movie, because
I've got something else to be nervous about."

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:23.060
2020 will also see Pattinson appear in the
anxiously awaited adaptation of Donald Ray

00:03:23.060 --> 00:03:26.000
Pollock's beloved novel The Devil All The
Time.

